Calculate the curl of the vector field $\vec{F}(x, y, z) = f(x, y, z)\uvec{i} + g(x, y, z)\uvec{j} + h(x, y, z)\uvec{k}$, where $f(x, y, z) = \sinh(x - z)$, $g(x, y, z) = (x + y)^3$, and $h(x, y, z) = \sqrt{z}$.

Solution:
The curl of the vector field $\vec{F}(x, y, z)$ is given by the following components:

$$
\nabla \times \vec{F} = \left\{
\begin{array}{c}
\frac{\partial h}{\partial y} - \frac{\partial g}{\partial z} \\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial z} - \frac{\partial h}{\partial x} \\
\frac{\partial g}{\partial x} - \frac{\partial f}{\partial y}
\end{array}
\right\}
$$

Substituting the given functions, we get:

$$
\nabla \times \vec{F} = \left\{
\begin{array}{c}
0 - 0 \\
\cosh(x - z) - 0 \\
3(x + y)^2 - (-\cosh(x - z))
\end{array}
\right\}
$$

Simplifying, the curl is:

$$
\nabla \times \vec{F} = \left\{
\begin{array}{c}
0 \\
\cosh(x - z) \\
3(x + y)^2 + \cosh(x - z)
\end{array}
\right\}
$$

